    "body": "Learned a bit here :) ... I now realize that the difference between flat tree order and shadow-including order is not whether the shadow DOM is included. Rather, it relates to the order of `slot`-related elements.\r\n\r\nI think what we want here is flat tree order since it [matches the top-level DOM](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scoping/#:~:text=the%20flat%20tree%20is%20the,dom%20tree) tree, includes the shadow DOM and traverses through `slot`s in a way that more [closely matches](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scoping/#:~:text=slots%20get%20filled%20with%20the%20nodes%20that%20are%20assigned%20to%20them) what is displayed/layout. I've updated the PR.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
