    "body": "> Or we could change the step that assembles _scrollers_, and then just use the normal list order? Something like this:\r\n> \r\n> > Let _scrollers_ be the [list](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list) obtained by performing a pre-order, depth-first traversal of _document_'s [flat tree](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scoping/#flat-tree), and filtering to keep only elements that establish a [scrolling box](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#scrolling-box).\r\n> > For each _scroller_ of _scrollers_:\r\n> \r\n\r\nThanks for the suggestion. Yes, pre-order depth-first traversal, which is [tree order](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order), is what we want. I've adopted this suggestion.\r\n\r\n> Also, it unfortunately looks like a merge conflict came into effect over the holidays. If you could try to resolve that, it would be appreciated; if it's giving you trouble though you can leave it to the editors.\r\n\r\nI believe I've been able to fix the conflicts.\r\n",
